# Micromagnetic Standard Problem 4 in mathlang — magnetization reversal of a
# 500 x 125 x 3 nm permalloy film. Built on libraries/mag.math (exchange + demag +
# Zeeman + RK4). The reversal dynamics reproduce mumax3 to ~1e-3 on the averages.
#
# CPU-bound: the demag FFT convolution runs every step, so the full run below is a
# couple of minutes — lower `nrev` to preview. `mag.relax` is a basic damping
# descent: it reaches a near-S-state but not the canonical one as precisely as
# mumax's adaptive minimizer (a conjugate-gradient minimizer is future work).
#
# View the result live with:  !animateField reversed
!include mag

# --- geometry & material (permalloy) ---
nx = 128
ny = 32
dx = 500e-9/nx
dy = 125e-9/ny
dz = 3e-9
Msat  = 800e3
Aex   = 13e-12
alpha = 0.02

# demag operator (kernel precomputed once)
demag = mag.demagOp(nx, ny, Msat, dx, dy, dz)

# --- 1) relax to (near) the S-state under exchange + demag, no applied field ---
heff0   = m -> mag.exchangeField(m, Aex, Msat, dx) + demag(m)
m_init  = vec.normalize(mag.bcast([1, 0.1, 0], nx, ny))
relaxed = mag.relax(m_init, heff0, 3e-3, 1500)
!print relaxed  m.avg = {round(mean(relaxed[.., .., 0]),4)}, {round(mean(relaxed[.., .., 1]),4)}

# --- 2) apply the reversal field and evolve (RK4) ---
Bext     = mag.bcast([-24.6e-3, 4.3e-3, 0], nx, ny)
heff     = m -> mag.exchangeField(m, Aex, Msat, dx) + demag(m) + Bext
nrev     = 500
reversed = mag.run(relaxed, heff, alpha, 1e-13, nrev)
!print reversed m.avg = {round(mean(reversed[.., .., 0]),4)}, {round(mean(reversed[.., .., 1]),4)}, {round(mean(reversed[.., .., 2]),4)}
